# {{name}}

A juiz component written in Haskell. It was made with `juiz pkg create --idl` of juiz {{juiz_version}},
from the process / container declarations of `{{idl_main}}`.

License: {{license}}

## What is inside

{{types_table}}

| Path | What it is |
| --- | --- |
| `{{idl_main}}` | The types and the declarations (JIDL) |
| `src/{{Name}}.hs` | The Component. Each function is a type, paired with its manifest and listed in `juizComponent`. Write the bodies (`error "…"`) |
| `gen/` | The Haskell types (record, enum) of the `.jidl`, generated by `scripts/dev.sh` (`juiz idl -g haskell`). Not in git |
| `{{name_kebab}}.cabal` | Builds the plugin `lib{{name}}` with a cabal `foreign-library` |
| `cabal.project` | Where hsjuiz (the Haskell library of juiz) and libjuiz_sdk are |
| `app/app.conf` | The configuration to start juiz with. It is also the entry of the `.juizapp` package |
| `app/juizapp.yaml` | The `.juizapp` manifest (name, version, required juiz version) |
| `scripts/dev.sh` | Build the plugin and put it in `app/plugins/<target>/` |
| `scripts/pack.sh` | Build, collect the libraries the plugin uses, and make `dist/{{name}}-<version>.juizapp` |
| `scripts/bundle-plugin-deps.sh` | Used by `scripts/pack.sh`. A copy of the script of the same name in juiz {{juiz_version}} |

## Requirements

Linux or macOS. Haskell plugins on Windows are not supported by this skeleton yet (juiz issue #137).

- juiz {{juiz_version}} (`juiz --version`). Install it with `cargo install juiz_app --version {{juiz_version}}` or `pip install juiz-cli=={{juiz_version}}`
- GHC 9.6 or later and cabal ([GHCup](https://www.haskell.org/ghcup/))
- libjuiz_sdk {{juiz_version}} in `{{juiz_sdk_dir}}`
- The juiz source of {{juiz_version}} for hsjuiz, in `{{hsjuiz_dir}}` (hsjuiz is not on Hackage yet)
- To make the package on Linux: patchelf (`apt install patchelf` or `pip install patchelf`)

`cabal.project` has the absolute paths of hsjuiz and libjuiz_sdk that `juiz pkg create` found or expected.
If you put them somewhere else, or share this project with someone, change the paths in `cabal.project`.

hsjuiz and libjuiz_sdk must be the same version as juiz: juiz does not load a plugin that carries another version of libjuiz_sdk.
`app/juizapp.yaml` requires `juiz: "={{juiz_version}}"` for the same reason.
When you update juiz, get hsjuiz and libjuiz_sdk of the new version, and change `cabal.project` and `app/juizapp.yaml`.

