The first build also builds hsjuiz, so it takes a while.
The plugin in `app/plugins/<target>/` uses the hsjuiz library in `dist-newstyle`: if you delete `dist-newstyle` or switch GHC, run `scripts/dev.sh` again.
The package made by `scripts/pack.sh` carries all the libraries the plugin uses, and runs without GHC.

If linking fails on macOS with `tapi error: ... unknown architecture`, the Command Line Tools are newer than the selected Xcode.
Build with `DEVELOPER_DIR=/Library/Developer/CommandLineTools scripts/dev.sh` (juiz issue #143).

## Changing the .jidl

`scripts/dev.sh` generates the Haskell types of `{{idl_main}}` in `gen/` before each build.
When you change the declarations, change the functions and the manifests in `src/{{Name}}.hs` and `app/app.conf` to match
(`juiz idl -g haskell-skeleton -o <dir> {{idl_main}}` writes the functions of all the declarations again, to copy from).
When the `.jidl` gets a new namespace, add its module to `other-modules` in `{{name_kebab}}.cabal`.

## Versions

The package version is `0.1.0` in both `{{name_kebab}}.cabal` and `app/juizapp.yaml`. When you release a new version, change both.

## Plugins for several OSes in one package

`scripts/pack.sh` collects the libraries for the OS it runs on.
For another OS (Linux or macOS), run `scripts/dev.sh` there, then
`scripts/bundle-plugin-deps.sh app/plugins/<target>/lib{{name}}.<so|dylib> <dir>`, and copy `<dir>` to `app/plugins/<target>/` on the machine that makes the package.
`scripts/pack.sh --no-build` packs those directories as they are.
